{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1555, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given a 2D integer matrix grid of size n x m, an integer array limits of length n, and an integer k. The task is to find the maximum sum of at most k elements from the matrix grid such that:\n\n\nThe number of elements taken from the i^th row of grid does not exceed limits[i].\n\n\nReturn the maximum sum.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: grid = [[1,2],[3,4]], limits = [1,2], k = 2\nOutput: 7\nExplanation:\n\nFrom the second row, we can take at most 2 elements. The elements taken are 4 and 3.\nThe maximum possible sum of at most 2 selected elements is 4 + 3 = 7.\n\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: grid = [[5,3,7],[8,2,6]], limits = [2,2], k = 3\nOutput: 21\nExplanation:\n\nFrom the first row, we can take at most 2 elements. The element taken is 7.\nFrom the second row, we can take at most 2 elements. The elements taken are 8 and 6.\nThe maximum possible sum of at most 3 selected elements is 7 + 8 + 6 = 21.\n\n\n \nConstraints:\n\nn == grid.length == limits.length\nm == grid[i].length\n1 <= n, m <= 500\n0 <= grid[i][j] <= 10^5\n0 <= limits[i] <= m\n0 <= k <= min(n * m, sum(limits))\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def maxSum(self, grid: List[List[int]], limits: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1609, "char_start": 1567, "quote": "Input:\n[[1, 2], [3, 4]]\n[1, 2]\n2\nOutput:\n7", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1670, "char_start": 1621, "quote": "Input:\n[[5, 3, 7], [8, 2, 6]]\n[2, 2]\n3\nOutput:\n21", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "f55c57d6c6c98b33774fd597b511eb6f4e4b9027167ba88e62edc9c44174330c", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "480def91750540a112057914674a7816a7474dc2fdf15d9e34bcaa0e2abf790a", "seq": 2}
